<title>UK: UK GDP rises revised 0.9 pct in Q1 1997.</title>
<headline>UK GDP rises revised 0.9 pct in Q1 1997.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics issued the following provisional, seasonally adjusted data on Gross Domestic Product (GDP) in the first quarter of 1997. (Index base 1990, constant prices, previous estimates in brackets)</p>
<p>				    Q1,97	   Q4,96	   Q1,96</p>
<p>    Index			 110.8 (110.8) 109.8 (109.8) 107.6</p>
<p>    Pct change on qtr	 0.9   (1.0)   0.8   (0.8)     0.6</p>
<p>    Pct change yr/yr	  3.0   (3.0)   2.6   (2.6)     2.1</p>
<p>IMPLIED GDP DEFLATOR AT FACTOR COST</p>
<p>    Index			 124.3	   123.5	   120.8</p>
<p>    Pct change on qtr	 0.6	     0.5		 0.9</p>
<p>    Pct change yr/yr	  2.8	     3.2		 2.3</p>
<p>GDP AT MARKET PRICES (MONEY GDP)</p>
<p>    Index			 138.9	   136.8	   131.3</p>
<p>    Pct change on qtr	 1.6	     1.7		 1.7</p>
<p>    Pct change yr/yr	  5.8	     6.0		 5.1</p>
<p>GDP EX OIL AND GAS EXTRACTION (constant prices)</p>
<p>    Index (base 1990)	 109.6 (109.6) 108.5 (108.5) 106.5</p>
<p>    Pct change on qtr	 1.0   (1.0)   0.8   (0.8)     0.6</p>
<p>    Pct change yr/yr	  2.9   (3.0)   2.5   (2.5)     2.2</p>
<p>CONSUMER SPENDING AT MARKET PRICES</p>
<p>    pct change qtr/qtr	1.0</p>
<p>    pct change qtr/yr ago   3.5</p>
<p>OUTPUT DATA</p>
<p>					   INDEX     Q1/Q4    Q197/Q196</p>
<p>    Mining, oil and gas	    143.9     -1.3	  2.2</p>
<p>    Electricity, gas and water   120.9     -2.8	 -1.2</p>
<p>    Manufacturing sector	   103.2	0.6	  1.6</p>
<p>    Total production		 108.1	0.1	  1.4</p>
<p>    Distribution,hotels,catering 110.3	0.9	  3.1</p>
<p>    Transport and communication  127.0	1.1	  3.6</p>
<p>    Business services &amp; finance  121.6	2.0	  6.7</p>
<p>    Total service industries     115.3	1.2	  3.9</p>
<p>GROSS FIXED CAPITAL FORMATION Q1</p>
<p>    pct change qtr/qtr	     3.3</p>
<p>    pct change qtr/yr ago qtr    4.3</p>
<p>GENERAL GOVT FINAL CONSUMPTION Q1</p>
<p>    pct change qtr/qtr	    -0.1</p>
<p>    pct change qtr/yr ago qtr    1.7</p>
<p>NOTE - market forecast for the second estimate of first quarter GDP was +1.0 pct qtr/qtr, 3.0 pct yr/yr -- the same as the original figures published on April 25.  </p>
<p>The ONS said the downward revision in the quarter-on-quarter GDP growth rate largely reflected industrial production figures already released.</p>
<p>Imports grew faster than exports over the quarter. Steady growth was seen in income from employment, largely driven by average earnings.</p>
</text>
